              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The URL `www.home.fedex.com/express` is an internal **intranet website** reserved exclusively for FedEx employees (specifically within the FedEx Express division). \n\n### Key Information Regarding This Link:\n\n* **Access is restricted:** Because this is an intranet site, it sits behind the FedEx corporate firewall. You **cannot** access this URL from a personal device, home internet connection, or mobile data unless you are using a company-issued device connected to the secure FedEx network or an authorized FedEx VPN. \n* **What it is used for:** For employees on-site, the `home.fedex.com` portal acts as a central hub where they can use search keywords to access employee tools, such as:\n  * **Dimensions / Kronos:** To check schedules, view timecards, and log hours.\n  * **Payroll / Workday:** To view pay stubs and manage employee information.\n  * **Internal Careers:** To search and apply for internal job postings.\n  * **Travelnet:** To view personal travel benefits and employee discounts.\n\n### How to Access the Tools You Need:\n* **If you are trying to access employee tools from home:** Many FedEx tools can be accessed externally using security verification (like Okta/PurpleID). You may need to navigate directly to the Okta sign-in page (`purpleid.okta.com`) rather than the intranet homepage to access specific apps like Workday on your personal phone or computer.\n* **If you are a customer:** If you are trying to track a package, schedule a pickup, or find a shipping location, you will need to go to the public-facing FedEx website: [www.fedex.com](https://www.fedex.com).",
